issue_context.body:
**Describe the bug**
I am doing a project with the MCU **STM32F091RC** and whenever I enable SHELL-UART through `CONFIG_SHELL=y` in the **prj.conf** file, the application stops working.

The application I am testing is below, just printing a `Hello World` and blinking an LED. Note that I do not create shell commands. I've just enabled it in the **prj.conf** file.

```
/*
 * Copyright (c) 2012-2014 Wind River Systems, Inc.
 *
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 */

#include <device.h>
#include <dfu/mcuboot.h>
#include <gpio.h>
#include <misc/printk.h>
#include <misc/reboot.h>
#include <zephyr.h>

#define LED_PORT DT_GPIO_LEDS_LED_GREEN_GPIO_CONTROLLER
#define LED DT_GPIO_LEDS_LED_GREEN_GPIO_PIN


void main(void)
{
    struct device *dev;
    u32_t led_value = 0;

    dev = device_get_binding(LED_PORT);
    /* Set LED pin as output */
    gpio_pin_configure(dev, LED, GPIO_DIR_OUT);

    while (1) {
        printk("Hello World! %s\n", CONFIG_BOARD);
        gpio_pin_write(dev, LED, led_value);
        led_value = !led_value;
        k_sleep(K_MSEC(200));
    }
}
```

The file **prj.conf** is like this:

```
CONFIG_PRINTK=y
CONFIG_SHELL=y
CONFIG_REBOOT=y
```

In the .**dts** file I have used this to choose UART console and shell:

``` 
chosen {
		zephyr,console = &usart2;
		zephyr,shell-uart = &usart2;
		zephyr,sram = &sram0;
		zephyr,flash = &flash0;
		zephyr,code-partition = &slot0_partition;
	};
```

I have uploaded the same code to **nRF52840_pca10056** board and everything works fine. Another board with **STM32F4** had the same result as the nRF board, application runs OK.

The only difference that breaks the normal execution of the application in the **STM32F0** is the change from `CONFIG_SHELL=y` to `CONFIG_SHELL=n`. It's like the application does not start and LED does not blink.

Does anyone have any idea on this?
